      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 1999 Academic Press.",
        "AbstractText": "Two patients with a history of stage IB cervical cancer who had undergone prior radical abdominal hysterectomy, omental J-flap placement, and postoperative whole pelvic radiation therapy required subsequent exploratory laparotomy with resection of omental J-flap for treatment of chronic abdominal pain 5 and 2 years, respectively, following J-flap placement. Issues relating to this unusual possible long-term complication of omentoplasty are discussed."
      },
